    {
      "id": "qrx097q",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Disease"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Diseases are broadly classified into communicable (infectious) and non-communicable (non-infectious) categories.",
        "Communicable diseases are caused by microscopic pathogens such as bacteria, viruses, fungi, and protozoa.",
        "Deficiency diseases result from a sustained lack of essential vitamins, minerals, or nutrients in daily dietary intake.",
        "The immune system offers two lines of defense: Innate immunity (nonspecific, present at birth) and Acquired immunity (specific, developed over time).",
        "Vaccination introduces weakened or inactivated pathogens to stimulate the production of antibodies without causing severe illness."
      ],
      "id": "eyjwx5w"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "btpabez",
      "content": "• A disease is a condition that impairs normal body function."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5sntk4u",
      "content": "• It may cause pain, weakness, discomfort or dysfunction of organs."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fymu63d",
      "content": "• Diseases may be infectious or non‑infectious."
    },
    {
      "id": "yumc1uh",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Types of Diseases"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6orzhf2",
      "content": "• Communicable diseases – Spread from one person to another."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "on2mjwp",
      "content": "• Non‑communicable diseases – Do not spread between individuals."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l8oe63o",
      "content": "• Deficiency diseases – Caused by lack of nutrients."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "awc4dq8",
      "content": "• Hereditary diseases – Passed through genes."
    },
    {
