    {
      "id": "t030ts2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Immune System"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ovkhkp5",
      "content": "• The immune system protects the body from pathogens."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hcoc401",
      "content": "• It includes white blood cells, antibodies and lymphatic organs."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Feature",
        "Communicable Diseases",
        "Non-Communicable Diseases"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Causative Agent",
          "Biological pathogens (Bacteria, Viruses, Protozoa, Fungi)",
          "Genetic factors, lifestyle habits, aging, or nutritional deficiencies"
        ],
        [
          "Transmission",
          "Transmitted from infected to healthy individual via air, water, food, or vectors",
          "Cannot be transmitted from one person to another"
        ],
        [
          "Onset & Duration",
          "Usually acute with rapid onset",
          "Typically chronic with gradual progression"
        ],
        [
          "Examples",
          "Tuberculosis, Cholera, Malaria, Influenza",
          "Diabetes, Hypertension, Cancer, Scurvy"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "aicq80d"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dzaoexq",
      "content": "• It identifies and destroys harmful microorganisms."
    },
    {
      "id": "s6jojyq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Types of Immunity"
    },
    {
