            "<p>Antibodies obtained from another source</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "994v27g",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Vaccination"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5ltkabo",
      "content": "• Vaccines stimulate the immune system to produce antibodies."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rogmhet",
      "content": "• They protect against diseases such as polio, measles and hepatitis."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "89of3f3",
      "content": "• Vaccination is one of the most effective methods of disease prevention."
    },
    {
      "id": "wil9wls",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Prevention of Diseases"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gcato29",
      "content": "• Maintain personal hygiene."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h8qkqe6",
      "content": "• Eat a balanced diet."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xlsck0h",
      "content": "• Drink clean water."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Differentiate clearly between Active Immunity (body produces its own antibodies) and Passive Immunity (ready-made antibodies introduced into the body).",
        "Memorize major nutritional deficiency diseases: Vitamin A (Night Blindness), Vitamin C (Scurvy), Vitamin D (Rickets), Iron (Anaemia), and Iodine (Goitre).",
        "Edward Jenner is frequently asked as the pioneer who developed the first successful smallpox vaccine in 1796.",
        "Disease vectors are crucial exam topics: Female Anopheles mosquito causes Malaria, while Aedes aegypti mosquito transmits Dengue and Chikungunya."
      ],
      "id": "evai84i"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s3z3wc0",
      "content": "• Regular vaccination."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xmiyeys",
      "content": "• Control insects and mosquitoes."
    },
    {
      "id": "vlmlnqk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nkl3c09",
      "content": "• Vaccines help build immunity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5dnt5mr",
      "content": "• Vitamin deficiencies cause several diseases."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z7lslaj",
      "content": "• Pathogens include bacteria, viruses, fungi and parasites."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p2vtggm",
      "content": "• The immune system defends the body against infections."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
